NeuralPath is a smart website that helps people understand their career value. It looks at a person's resume
Home Page: This is the first thing users see. it explains that the site uses high-tech tools to help their careers.
Login/Signup: Users create an account (called a "Neural Node") with a username and password to keep their information safe.
Upload Page: Users click a button to upload their resume file (like a PDF).
Scanning Page: While the computer reads the resume, the user sees a cool "scanning" animation. This makes the site feel advanced.
Dashboard (The Report): This is the final page. It shows:
Strengths: What the user is great at.
Weaknesses: What the user needs to improve.
Opportunities: Better jobs they could get.
Risks: If their job might be replaced by AI in the future.
The Tools Used (Tech Stack)
The Look (Frontend): I used HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. This makes the site look dark and futuristic, like a high-tech lab.
The Brain (Backend): The site is built to work with Python. Python is used to read the resume and understand the words.
The AI: The system connects to powerful AI models (like GPT or Gemini) to give career advice.
The Storage (Database): I use MySQL or PostgreSQL to save the user's account and their career reports.
Most resume tools only check for spelling. This tool actually thinks like a career coach. it helps users stay ahead of the competition and get higher-paying jobs.
